implementationPlan.description:
Docs (DoD 3), edited with the Edit tool only.
(a) docs/MCP_SERVER.md, the '### moe.lease_account' Notes. After the bullet that starts '`accountId: null` means wait' (:3173), add one bullet. It says:
- every call counts as presence for the calling seat, whatever it returns;
- it refreshes the seat's `lastActivityAt` and writes `Worker.accountId` only when it changes;
- an unknown `workerId` gets no worker record, and a DEAD seat is not refreshed;
- so a task held through `MOE_ACCOUNT_WAIT` stays held. The wrapper leases again at most `MOE_ACCOUNT_RETRY_SEC` (default 300 s) apart, inside the default `reviewStaleTimeoutMs` (30 min), so the REVIEW self-heal does not release a waiting QA seat's row.
(b) scripts/CLAUDE.md, the 'Claude account rotation' bullet (:42, one physical line). Right after '(default 300), the task held', insert: ': each `moe.lease_account` call counts as the seat's presence (it refreshes `lastActivityAt`), so the REVIEW self-heal leaves a waiting QA seat's row held'.
- Change nothing else on that line or any other.
- task-e3e81c45 edits the adjacent line 43. This row dependsOn it, so this worktree's base already holds that edit and the landing merge stays clean (planningNotes).
